<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedĭfĭcātōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>pertaining to building.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedificatoria somnia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 47</span></i>
			.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedĭfĭcātōrĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., = architectura,
			Boëth. Aristot. Top. 3, 1, p. 680.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Fig.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbum aedificatorium mortis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>that was the cause of death</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Carn. Christ. 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
